Z||000000||rockcrawl||05-10-2001||08:33 PM||||Driving through Doylestown area today and almost broke my neck when I spotted two Fieros sitting in front of Midas on rt 611. I quick pulled a U-turn to check out the convertible notchback. It was in pretty rough shape but it looked like a professional one-off conversion. It looked like there was no top intended (tarp bundled in passenger seat), just a smooth fiberglass pannel over the back and a cap on the windshield header. Damn, I wish I had my digi camera along.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> As I pulled out I realised I hadn't even checked out the frame stiffening.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||14
